  { q: 'What is the molar mass of water?', a: '18.015 grams per mole. It is two hydrogen atoms at 1.008 each plus one oxygen at 15.999, which sums to 18.015. The Best Answer Hub Molecular Weight Calculator returns this with the per-element breakdown, so you can see exactly where the number comes from rather than just trusting it.' },
  { q: 'What is the difference between molar mass and molecular weight?', a: 'In practice they are the same number and used interchangeably. Molecular weight is technically a dimensionless ratio, while molar mass carries units of grams per mole, but the value is identical. The Best Answer Hub Molecular Weight Calculator returns g/mol, the unit used in stoichiometry and solution preparation.' },
